courses.learning_outcomes:
At the end of the course, students will:
- understand the relationship between psychological development of children and language learning;

- articulate the relationship between the properties of Chinese Language and the development of language ability;

- know how to apply the knowledge of linguistic in teaching Chinese Language;

- articulate the basic principles of language ability development.

At the end of the course, students will be able to:

- understand the relationship between language and though;

- understand the relationship between thought and writing;

- understand the development of train of thought in articles;

- revise the article structure through analyzing its train of thought:

- enhance their analytical skill;

- enhance their writing skill though writing exercises.

At the end of the course, students will be able to:

- master the fundamental theories of using Putonghua as a medium of instruction in teaching Chinese;

- deepen their understanding in the curriculum integration and current development of using Putonghua as a medium of instruction in teaching Chinese through discussions;

- conclude an ideal mode of using Putonghua as a medium of instruction in teaching Chinese through research and study, and practical experiences.

At the end of the course, students will be able to:

- Master the natures, teaching aims and characteristics of using Putonghua as a medium of instruction in teaching Chinese;

- Master the principles and methodologies in listening and speaking teaching;

- Master the principles and methodologies in reading and writing teaching;

- Master the principles and methodologies in reading aloud teaching;

- Master the principles and methodologies in the phonetic transcription (Hangyu Pinyin) teaching.

At the end of the course, students will be able to:

- understand the relationship between language development and cognitive development and the application in curriculum design;

- understand the difference between spoken and written language, and the application in teaching;

- understand the effect of the teachers' oral proficiency on students' language ability;

- develop the basic oral expression skills such as pause, stress pattern, speech rate and intonation; develop the abiltiy to manipulate the articulator; master the complementary use of body language and spoken language; and master the use of Cantonese as the basis of medium of instruction to build up a good example in learning language;

- develop skills for the purposes of narrating and describing, reading aloud, explanation, questioning, and debating, and apply the skills in classroom teaching.
